    board: repair CF-117 + CF-118 AC1 — count-relative probe assertions, no absolute row counts. Addresses CF-117, CF-118.
    
    The Tier 2 judge on CF-117-QA1 (verdict 2c542a5d, PASS on legs 1 and 4, FAIL on legs 2 and 3) rejected the
    filing for a real defect in my own criteria: AC1 of both rows quoted row counts measured on the pre-filing
    90-row board (`FAIL board rows — 91 vs 90 rows; 1 divergent ids: CF-999` and `PASS board rows — 90 vs 90
    rows; 0 divergent ids: none`). Those literals cannot reproduce once the board grows — the judge itself
    measured `93 vs 92` and `92 vs 92` on the committed tree. The probes were correct; the acceptance text
    baked a moving number into a falsifiable criterion.
    
    Repair, board-only and byte-preserving outside the two target lines: AC1 of each row now states the SHAPE
    the probe must print (`N+1 vs N rows; 1 divergent ids: CF-999` for CF-117, `N vs N rows; 0 divergent ids:
    none` for CF-118) and keeps the stable, load-bearing parts as literals — the named id CF-999, the
    `named_ids=0` line, and `drift_rc=1`. Two `task_updated` events (ids 130, 131) record the reason. Every
    other board line is byte-identical; line count unchanged at 92 rows / 131 events.
    
    Re-run at this tree: both probes print the required shapes (93 vs 92 with CF-999 named; 92 vs 92 with
    named_ids=0 and drift_rc=1). Gates: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (rc 0); scripts/boardctl
    validate -> RESULT: OK (33 warnings, all pre-existing classes plus the probe-outside-canon class these
    rows carry).
    
    Hook note: this is the clone transport (four sibling lanes were `running` against the shared checkout),
    and the clone carries no installed commit hook, so the guard did not run here; the graded gate is the
    explicit `gitreins task complete CF-117-QA2` run on this tree. The superseded verdict 2c542a5d is kept in
    .gitreins/history as evidence of the criterion defect, not deleted.
    
