 {"id":"CF-115","title":"P4 — the CF-099 drift probe certifies two legs it never measures: a milestone with no open-defect list prints OK, and the acceptance plan reverse table is never read","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:03:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:03:56Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"9fa9cfa69257639c4d6c3e00ec68a7510da05228a83f9eade263365d6444106d"},"reasoning":"Measured at 6e8621f from a clean clone of origin/main. Arm A: rewording the PRD milestone phrase \"open defects on this path are\" to \"remaining gaps on this path are\" (a pure prose edit) makes docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exit 0, print \"open_blockers=\" empty and still print OK agree at HEAD, because the open-blocker leg is keyed on sed -n \"s/.*open defects//p\" and an absent phrase makes the loop body vacuous. Arm D: deleting the acceptance plan reverse-direction table row for sections 22-28 (22 table rows to 21) leaves the probe at exit 0 with the same OK line, because the probe never opens that table although AC4 of CF-099 requires an entry for every selftest section. Control arm B: inserting a COMPLETE id into the open-defect list exits 1 with DRIFT naming that id, so the instrument works where it is wired. Distinct from CF-113 (the reverse-mapping CONTENT is false because the section census cannot see lettered sub-arms) and from CF-069 (the selftest board arm is fail-open): this is the probe certifying legs it does not evaluate.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce at the current tree from the repository root: the probe field of this row prints a measured line whose open_blockers= value is empty, then probe_rc=0, on a clone whose PRD milestone phrase was reworded and whose acceptance-plan reverse table lost its sections 22-28 row.\n1. docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exits nonzero and names BOTH legs: a milestone Status block with no open-defect phrase (or an empty list after it) is reported as DRIFT, and any selftest section with no