 {"id":"CF-116","title":"P3 \u2014 the census coverage assertion counts rows, so a mid-run insert mints a duplicate plus a missing row with received == total and the recipe still exits 0","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:20:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:20:00Z","reasoning":["Measured 2026-11-03 by the docs-QA lane at 0c765f6 with the committed stand-in docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py, which models a project inserted between the two page fetches: page offset=0 serves rows 0..499 of a 600-row list, then the list shifts by one, so page offset=500 serves row 499 a second time and never serves row 500. BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh prints the count line 600 and 600 row lines and exits 0, while the output holds 599 distinct rows, has no code-factory-p500 line and prints code-factory-p499 twice. CF-089's accepted fix compares received rows against the first reported total (tests/selftest.sh arm 25, fixture mode=short, 'rows received=865 != total reported=866'); that assertion is satisfied exactly by this shape. The row's own trigger class \u2014 a scheduler restart or load-shed between two pages \u2014 also covers an insert between two pages, because offset pagination over a list that mutates mid-run shifts every later offset. Nothing in the tree enumerates identities: the count line comes from wc -l over rows appended blindly with jq -c '.projects[]'. Scheduler project rows carry id=null (GET /api/v1/projects?limit=1), so the identity key is .name."],"acceptance_criteria":["1. Reproduce at the current tree: the probe prints census_rc=0, row_lines=600, distinct_rows=599, p500=MISSING, p499_occurrences=2 \u2014 a complete-looking census that dropped one row and counted another twice. 2. The census asserts identity coverage, not just count: it refuses with a named message and a nonzero exit when an enumerated .name repeats or the distinct count is below the reported total, naming the measured numbers (distinct, duplicates, total) and one concrete duplicated or missing identity. The README.md fence under 'The lanes' and docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh carry the same change and stay textually identical. 3. A tests/selftest.sh arm proves the check can fail: a fixture mode that serves the duplicated boundary row plus the hole prints the named refusal at exit 1 with no census printed, while arms 22-25 still pass unchanged. 4. The live scheduler census still prints 19 rows and exits 0; bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS; scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK."],"probe":"(timeout 40 python3 docs/audits/cf116-census-dup-standin.py --port 18996 >/dev/null 2>&1 &); sleep 2; BASE=http://127.0.0.1:18996 bash docs/audits/cf089-census-recipe.sh >/tmp/cf116-census.out 2>&1; echo \"census_rc=$?\"; echo \"row_lines=$(grep -c '^code-factory-p' /tmp/cf116-census.out)\"; echo \"distinct_rows=$(grep '^code-factory-p' /tmp/cf116-census.out | sort -u | wc -l)\"; if grep -q '^code-factory-p500 ' /tmp/cf116-census.out; then echo \"p500=present\"; else echo \"p500=MISSING\"; fi; echo \"p499_occurrences=$(grep -c '^code-factory-p499 ' /tmp/cf116-census.out)\"","detail":{"filed_by":"code-factory-docs-qa-2026-11-03-19-51-49","reproduced_at":"0c765f6"}}
-{"id":"CF-117","title":"P3 \u2014 the publish-drift census cannot tell a workdir that is merely AHEAD from one that is stale and lossy, so the CF-114 check reds the normal mid-tick state and no gate can run it","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-03T20:30:36Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T20:30:36Z","detail":{"evidence":[]},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 15:2x -05 by the QA lane at origin/main 25d1e71. scripts/board_drift.py:146-147 computes extra = work_rows.keys() - pub_rows.keys() and :155 reports report.row(not extra, 'board extra ids', ...), while :157-162 additionally fails the row-count row on any all_ids non-empty. A canonical checkout that has just appended an uncommitted row \u2014 the state every board commit begins from \u2014 is therefore 'extra': probe output today is `FAIL byte parity tasks.jsonl \u2014 bytes differ`, `FAIL board extra ids \u2014 CF-999`, `FAIL board rows \u2014 91 vs 90 rows; 1 divergent ids: CF-999`, `RESULT: DRIFT (3 failed)`, rc=1. The CF-114 red fixture (one row reopened, one row deleted) prints the SAME verdict word, the same rc, and no direction field, so an operator cannot separate 'one unpushed new row' from 'a stale copy that reverts five closures' (CF-114's P2 defect). Consequences: (a) nothing calls the census except tests/selftest.sh:943 and docs/BOARD.md:47 \u2014 grep for board_drift over *.sh/*.py/*.yaml/*.toml outside those two files returns nothing, so the guard's test_command (bash tests/selftest.sh) and scripts/boardctl validate both green a stale workdir; (b) wiring it in as-is would refuse every board commit, because the commit is always made from an ahead workdir. That makes the CF-114 protection advisory, and a check whose DRIFT verdict is the normal state is decoration by AGENTS.md rule 2.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce on the current tree: the row probe prints `FAIL board extra ids \u2014 CF-999`, `FAIL board rows \u2014 91 vs 90 rows; 1 divergent ids: CF-999` and `drift_rc=1` for a workdir that removed and reverted nothing.\n2. The census classifies DIRECTION: a workdir whose id set is a strict superset of the published id set with no status reversal is reported as pending publication (the added ids named in the row, exit 0), while any status reversal or published id missing from the workdir still prints a FAIL naming those ids and exits 1. Both classifications name the measured counts (added, missing, reversed).\n3. tests/selftest.sh arm 29 gains fixture modes proving both directions: an `ahead` fixture (one added row, nothing reverted) exits 0 and names the added id, while the existing `red` fixture (reopened + deleted) still exits 1 and still names both ids; bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.\n4. docs/BOARD.md states the direction semantics and the single command, and scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK at the fixed tip.","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board\" \"$d/p\"; cp .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl \"$d/p/\"; cp \"$d/p/tasks.jsonl\" \"$d/p/events.jsonl\" \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board/\"; printf '%s\\n' '{\"id\":\"CF-999\",\"title\":\"an uncommitted new row\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"priority\":\"P4\",\"complexity\":1,\"reasoning\":\"r\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"a\"}' >> \"$d/w/.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl\"; out=$(python3 scripts/board_drift.py check --workdir \"$d/w\" --published-dir \"$d/p\" 2>&1); rc=$?; echo \"$out\" | grep -E 'FAIL|RESULT'; echo \"drift_rc=$rc\""}
